node3 (AlmaLinux 9.6) as systemd services with static bootstrap over the private network, with firewalld ports 2379/2380 opened. Verified cross-node replication (write on node1, read on node2/node3), verified continued read/write availability with quorum (2/3) while node3 was stopped, and verified node3 caught up on the missed key after rejoining. Then completed the mandatory sequential single-node-restart protocol on all three nodes (native systemctl reboot, one at a time, quorum preserved throughout), proving changed boot_id and full data/cluster-membership/quorum recovery after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Confirmed AlmaLinux 9.6 on all three nodes; no etcd pre-installed\",\"Downloaded and installed etcd/etcdctl/etcdutl v3.5.17 static binaries to /usr/local/bin on node1, node2, node3\",\"Created etcd system user and /var/lib/etcd data dir on each node\",\"Wrote per-node /etc/etcd/etcd.conf with static 3-member initial-cluster config (node1/node2/node3 peer+client URLs on NODE_IP)\",\"Created systemd unit /etc/systemd/system/etcd.service (Type=notify) on each node\",\"Opened firewalld ports 2379/2380 (tcp) permanently on each node and reloaded\",\"Enabled and started etcd on all three nodes; confirmed cluster formed with 3 started members via member list\",\"Verified endpoint health across all three endpoints\",\"Wrote key benchkey via node1 endpoint, read successfully via node2 and node3 endpoints\",\"Stopped etcd on node3 to simulate member unavailability\",\"Wrote key duringoutage via node1 while node3 was down; confirmed read via node2; confirmed 2-node endpoint health during outage\",\"Restarted etcd on node3; confirmed it caught up and could read both benchkey and duringoutage; confirmed 3/3 cluster health and member list restored\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and etcd/data health proof on all three nodes\",\"Sequentially restarted node1, node2, node3 via systemctl reboot (one at a time), polled each until reachable again, confirmed changed boot_id, and confirmed etcd active with full data intact and cluster quorum/health/member-list restored after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-member etcd cluster formed across node1/node2/node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-513e489b96da4782\"],\"summary\":\"member list shows all 3 members (node1, node2, node3) with status started, matching peer/client addrs\"},{\"requirement\":\"Key written through one member is readable from others\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d3d01ac66fb141e7\",\"cmd-bd52ac1563c44c87\",\"cmd-b06f20710e7d4d5b\"],\"summary\":\"benchkey written via node1 endpoint, read back successfully via node2 and node3 endpoints\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster continues serving reads/writes while one member is unavailable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-537e305a2abb4547\",\"cmd-90633826091c4d09\",\"cmd-275c4221b1cb4b97\"],\"summary\":\"node3 etcd stopped; write to duringoutage succeeded via node1 and 2-node endpoint health check passed; read succeeded via node2, proving quorum (2/3) maintained availability\"},{\"requirement\":\"Unavailable member catches up when brought back\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d42ab93696e34143\",\"cmd-980a4215ab934bb9\"],\"summary\":\"node3 etcd restarted; it successfully read both duringoutage and benchkey and cluster health/member-list returned to full 3/3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e78c3e18a282433b\",\"cmd-16951b345e64472f\",\"cmd-65f0161e78774af9\",\"cmd-d05f7f54d05b48f4\"],\"summary\":\"baseline boot_id f54d7366...; reboot issued (stream closed); post-reboot boot_id 2b5efe1f... with uptime 0 min; etcd active, data intact, cluster fully healthy after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6ddefe1ad375484b\",\"cmd-fe0fe84e78804ed4\",\"cmd-db8d50143f6342ba\",\"cmd-35a2e3d81da54731\"],\"summary\":\"baseline boot_id 717db5a2...; reboot issued (stream closed); post-reboot boot_id 586e5358... with uptime 0 min; etcd active, data intact, cluster fully healthy after restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-399783fee34e4927\",\"cmd-3d3cb494a47f4bdb\",\"cmd-36d537db95aa44ba\",\"cmd-481254fa9f584823\"],\"summary\":\"baseline boot_id 84419b90...; reboot issued (stream closed); post-reboot boot_id 568aba82... with uptime 0 min; etcd active, data intact, full 3/3 cluster health, single leader, matching raft applied index across all members\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-member etcd v3.5.17 cluster across node1/node2/node3 (AlmaLinux 9.6) as systemd services with static bootstrap over the private network, with firewalld ports 2379/2380 opened. Verified cross-node replication (write on node1, read on node2/node3), verified continued read/write availability with quorum (2/3) while node3 was stopped, and verified node3 caught up on the missed key after rejoining. Then completed the mandatory sequential single-node-restart protocol on all three nodes (native systemctl reboot, one at a time, quorum preserved throughout), proving changed boot_id and full data/cluster-membership/quorum recovery after each restart.","actions_performed":["Confirmed AlmaLinux 9.6 on all three nodes; no etcd pre-installed","Downloaded and installed etcd/etcdctl/etcdutl v3.5.17 static binaries to /usr/local/bin on node1, node2, node3","Created etcd system user and /var/lib/etcd data dir on each node","Wrote per-node /etc/etcd/etcd.conf with static 3-member initial-cluster config (node1/node2/node3 peer+client URLs on NODE_IP)","Created systemd unit /etc/systemd/system/etcd.service (Type=notify) on each node","Opened firewalld ports 2379/2380 (tcp) permanently on each node and reloaded","Enabled and started etcd on all three nodes; confirmed cluster formed with 3 started members via member list","Verified endpoint health across all three endpoints","Wrote key benchkey via node1 endpoint, read successfully via node2 and node3 endpoints","Stopped etcd on node3 to simulate member unavailability","Wrote key duringoutage via node1 while node3 was down; confirmed read via node2; confirmed 2-node endpoint health during outage","Restarted etcd on node3; confirmed it caught up and could read both benchkey and duringoutage; confirmed 3/3 cluster health and member list restored","Captured baseline boot_id and etcd/data health proof on all three nodes","Sequentially restarted node1, node2, node3 via systemctl reboot (one at a time), polled each until reachable again, confirmed changed boot_id, and confirmed etcd active with full data intact and cluster quorum/health/member-list restored after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-member etcd cluster formed across node1/node2/node3","command_ids":["cmd-513e489b96da4782"],"summary":"member list shows all 3 members (node1, node2, node3) with status started, matching peer/client addrs"},{"requirement":"Key written through one member is readable from others","command_ids":["cmd-d3d01ac66fb141e7","cmd-bd52ac1563c44c87","cmd-b06f20710e7d4d5b"],"summary":"benchkey written via node1 endpoint, read back successfully via node2 and node3 endpoints"},{"requirement":"Cluster continues serving reads/writes while one member is unavailable","command_ids":["cmd-537e305a2abb4547","cmd-90633826091c4d09","cmd-275c4221b1cb4b97"],"summary":"node3 etcd stopped; write to duringoutage succeeded via node1 and 2-node endpoint health check passed; read succeeded via node2, proving quorum (2/3) maintained availability"},{"requirement":"Unavailable member catches up when brought back","command_ids":["cmd-d42ab93696e34143","cmd-980a4215ab934bb9"],"summary":"node3 etcd restarted; it successfully read both duringoutage and benchkey and cluster health/member-list returned to full 3/3"},{"requirement":"node1 restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovery","command_ids":["cmd-e78c3e18a282433b","cmd-16951b